 saturated) and rises toward the cap when short — which a fixed price structurally
 cannot.
 
+**Per-ISO gate (RC-1B item 1).** The CR-1 gate is resolved through one seam,
+`constants.resolve_capacity_market_clearing(config, iso)`, which every
+capacity-price call site reads (`MarketDesign.capacity_price_per_firm_mw_yr`,
+`capacity_revenue_per_mw_yr`, `estimate_capacity_value`, the plant-financials
+report, and the runner's curve-reserve-position gate — rule 19). A per-ISO
+override, `ScenarioConfig.capacity_market_clearing_by_iso: dict[str, bool] |
+None`, arms/disarms the curve for a *named* ISO independently of the scalar
+`capacity_market_clearing`; the scalar governs any ISO the mapping does not name
+(and every ISO when the mapping is `None`, the default → byte-identical). This
+lets a probe arm CR-1 for one ISO — e.g. the capacity-hindcast harness's own ISO
+(`scripts/run_capacity_hindcast.py --capacity-market-clearing` sets
+`{iso: True}`) — with no leakage to the others.
+
+**Per-delivery-year vintage (RC-1B item 2).** The CR-1 curve and its net-CONE
+dollar anchor are resolved for the *run's delivery year* through
+`constants.resolve_demand_curve_vintage(iso, year)` over
+`MARKET_DESIGN_VINTAGES` (one `MarketDesign` per delivery year on disk in the
+`capacity-market-demand-curve` datatype: PJM 2021/22–2027/28, NYISO
+2021-22–2025-26, ISO-NE 2020/21–2027/28, MISO 2025-26 + 2026-27). Calendar year
+`Y` maps to the delivery year whose first year `== Y`; a year below the earliest
+vintage holds first (MISO's pre-RBDC 2021–2024 years, a vertical curve with no
+published net-CONE, serve the 2025-26 params), a year above the latest holds
+last. A vintage lacking a normalizable published shape (VRR points in absolute
+MW with no requirement-MW row, or a missing price-cap row) carries
+`demand_curve=()` and prices at its own **flat** published net-CONE anchor
+(rule 13 — never a fabricated curve point). The vintage table is consulted
+**only** when the gate is on and both `iso` and `year` are passed *and* a reserve
+position is supplied (the storage-entry screen is the wiring that passes both);
+every other call site passes no `year` and the fixed/default path never reads the
+table, so the default is byte-identical. The vintage entry for each registry
+curve's own delivery year reproduces that registry curve exactly (PJM 2026/27,
+NYISO 2025-26, NEISO 2027-28, MISO 2025-26), asserted in
+`tests/test_capacity_demand_curve.py`.
+
 Every curve number is a **published market-design parameter** (rule 13 — never a
 fit target), sourced from the `capacity-market-demand-curve` datatype
 (`data/raw/capacity-market/demand-curve`): PJM's VRR points + Net CONE + price
